    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="pm_d12">

                <pb facs="pm_d12-1" n="1" xml:id="pm_d12-1"/>

                <head>PM–12. Telegram from the Acting Secretary of State to the Embassy in
                        Panama<anchor n="1" xml:id="pm_d12-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1959-04-06T18:14:00-05:00">April 6, 1959,
                            6:14 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>338. For Ambassador.</p>
                <p>Deliver following message to President de la Guardia. Inform Department date and
                    time of delivery:</p>
                <p rendition="#right">April 6, 1959</p>
                <p>“Dear Mr. President:</p>
                <p>I have carefully read your letter and enclosed memorandum of March
                        seventh,<anchor n="2" xml:id="pm_d12-f2"/> which were personally delivered
                    to me by His Excellency Ambassador Ricardo Arias on March nineteenth.</p>
                <p>In your letter you refer to the manner in which the United States is implementing
                    the provisions of Item 1 of the Memorandum of Understandings Reached attached to
                    the Treaty of Mutual Understanding and Cooperation, entered into by Panama and
                    the United States in 1955.</p>
                <p>I understand the importance of the matters which you so frankly and forthrightly
                    present for my attention involving and affecting the close and friendly
                    relations that exist between <pb facs="pm_d12-2" n="2" type="facsimile"
                        xml:id="pm_d12-2"/> our two countries.</p>
                <p>As I am deeply interested in the status of relations between Panama and the
                    United States and your statements are of such import, I have asked the
                    appropriate agencies within this Government to undertake a careful and detailed
                    study of the problems you present. The determinations made as a result of these
                    studies will be made known to you and your Government at an early date.</p>
                <p>I extend my warmest personal regards to you, Mr. President, and to your
                    Government and the Panamanian people.</p>
                <p>Sincerely,</p>
                <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#bold">Dwight D. Eisenhower”</hi></p>
                <p>White House does not desire make foregoing public. Notify Department as much as
                    possible in advance should de la Guardia wish do so.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="pm_d12-f3"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Herter</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#pm_d12-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="pm_d12-f1-content">
